# Local development environment bindings — EXAMPLE.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` at the project root (that file is gitignored and
# never committed) and fill in what you need. See README "Local environment
# setup" and docs/MARKETING_ANALYTICS.md.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. The vendor ids below are PUBLIC values (they appear
# in any site's page source). Never put a token, API key or server-side
# credential in this file or in the marketing bindings — they are not read by
# the marketing layer.

# Unlocks local-only fallbacks: the guest-order-token secret fallback, and the
# console email adapter (which prints reset links to this terminal instead of
# sending real email — no real provider is integrated yet). NEVER set this in a
# deployed environment.
ENVIRONMENT=development

# Optional: override the local guest-order-token secret explicitly instead of
# relying on the built-in dev fallback. Not required for local dev to work.
# GUEST_ORDER_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consent-aware marketing analytics (src/marketing/*, public/static/analytics.js)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OFF unless you set MARKETING_TRACKING_ENABLED=1. With tracking on, each id
# below is validated against a strict allowlisted shape; an invalid value
# disables ONLY that adapter (fail closed) and shows a diagnostic at
# /admin/marketing. Leave a line commented out to keep that integration off.

# The master switch. Anything other than 1/true/yes/on (or absent) = off.
# MARKETING_TRACKING_ENABLED=1

# Meta Pixel id — 15–16 digits.
# META_PIXEL_ID=

# TikTok Pixel id — exactly 20 uppercase alphanumeric characters.
# TIKTOK_PIXEL_ID=

# GA4 measurement id — "G-" followed by 6–14 uppercase alphanumerics.
# GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Google Ads id — "AW-" followed by 6–12 digits.
# GOOGLE_ADS_ID=AW-0000000000

# Google Ads conversion label (Purchase only) — [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}.
# GOOGLE_ADS_PURCHASE_LABEL=

# Development-only: lets the automated browser journey observe the
# consent-gated request behaviour. Ignored unless ENVIRONMENT=development.
# MARKETING_ALLOW_AUTOMATION=1

# Verified-payment-phase switch for Purchase tracking. INERT on its own — do not
# set it yet (see docs/MARKETING_ANALYTICS.md §6).
# MARKETING_PURCHASE_TRACKING=1
